      "message": "fix(import): a STEP import reports the chord error of the mesh it kept\n\nThe refinement schedule moves to step_refine::refine, which returns the\nkept mesh with its own chord tolerance: a pass dropped for crossing the\nfacet budget no longer leaves the halved tolerance on the coarser mesh\n(the log under-reported the error, and said nothing when the halved\nvalue hit the target). step::parse_with_chord returns the mesh and the\ncoarsest kept tolerance in mm, refusing a non-finite or negative value;\nstep::parse is unchanged (same schedule, same meshes). A thread-local\ntest-only budget override forces a small fixture over budget.\n\nHeld work: the UI/MCP flag and the law tightening are escalated to\neffort:max on the issue.\n\nRefs #864\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
