        "date": "2026-11-11T20:29:00Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim,app): flag a STEP model imported coarser than promised; tighten its gouge verdicts, refuse past that\n\nA STEP model whose kept mesh is coarser than the importer's 0.005 mm\npromise used to import with only a stderr line. Its facets stand inside\nthe true surface on a convex wall, so a real gouge up to the mesh's error\ncould pass every verdict.\n\n- Flag: the import's achieved error lands on the model as\n  schema::ReducedFidelity (only above the cap), through ImportModel,\n  UpdateModel, ImportFixture and AddFixtureModel; kept by a repair,\n  restored by undo; saved as `coarse_mm` on that entity only. Shown on the\n  model page and the import status line, and by MCP import_model/get_job.\n- Tighten: VerifyContext::model_excess (achieved error less the cap),\n  apart from gouge_tol. Laws (b), (b2) and (f), contain_into, the lathe\n  axial hole verdict and the program sim's deviation tolerance subtract it\n  while a positive tolerance is left.\n- Refuse: past that the laws read untightened and the program gate refuses\n  the operation by name; the program sim does not judge. Kinds whose gouge\n  laws do not read the excess yet are refused on any reduced model.\n- A reduced-fidelity fixture is judged by its box grown by its error and\n  never acquitted by its mesh.\n\nWith no flag every law, golden and saved byte is unchanged. A metre-unit\nSTEP file (0.01 mm at the kernel's floor since #839) gets the same flag and\ntreatment. Owed work is #904.\n\nFixes #864\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
