        "date": "2026-11-12T02:33:55Z"
      },
      "message": "test(verify): the whole-arc wall reading answers to the tightened floor\n\nAfter the merge of main (#942): law (b)'s whole-arc reading takes the same\nfloor as the joints, so a reduced-fidelity model's excess tightens it too.\nPinned beside boundary_arc_walls: a corner between an arc's joints is\nconvicted between the plain and the tightened floor on a coarse model,\nclean at full fidelity and outside the tightened floor. The suite's\ncontext (new on main) takes the struct-update base for model_excess, which\nthe merge commit alone lacks.\n\nRefs #864\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
